Website Learning / Source Ingestion Requirement

FREEOS already has Phase 3 web research through SearXNG and public page reading. The Doctrine + Expert Training Layer must connect to that research layer so FREEOS can learn from websites in a controlled approval-based way.

Add website-to-doctrine ingestion.

Required flow:
1. User provides a URL or selects an existing research result.
2. FREEOS reads the public page using the existing research/page reader.
3. FREEOS extracts:
   - page title
   - URL
   - domain
   - author if detectable
   - publish/update date if detectable
   - key claims
   - key lessons
   - caveats
   - source type
   - relevant doctrine domain
   - proposed trust level
4. FREEOS must not automatically accept website content as truth.
5. FREEOS must create doctrine proposals from website content.
6. Drew must approve doctrine proposals before they become durable doctrine.
7. FREEOS must preserve source URL and evidence metadata with every doctrine proposal.
8. FREEOS must support creating training lessons from website content.
9. FREEOS must support creating rejected claims from website content if Drew rejects them.
10. FREEOS must not crawl entire websites automatically.
11. FREEOS must not bypass logins, paywalls, captchas, robots restrictions, or private pages.
12. FREEOS must not treat low-quality websites as high-trust sources automatically.

